    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d765">

                <pb facs="0896" n="800" xml:id="pg800"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.11/3736a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Reval</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Albrecht</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-25T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25, 1921—3
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Deliver following message to Litvinov<anchor n="6" xml:id="d765-f1"/> and
                    telegraph Department when it has been done: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The American Government is advised that, despite the repeated efforts of
                            Doctor Nansen in its behalf to secure the release of the American
                            prisoners in Russia, they are still held and in the most serious plight.
                            In the name of humanity the American Government demands of the Soviet
                            authorities that these prisoners be at once released. It is manifestly
                            impossible for the American authorities to countenance measures for the
                            relief of distress in Russia while our citizens are thus detained.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Advise Commissioner, Riga.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d765-f1" n="6" xml:id="d765-f1-content">
                <p>Maxim M. Litvinov, Assistant Soviet Commissar for Foreign Affairs and
                    Plenipotentiary Representative of the Soviet Republic to Esthonia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
